-- Whole numbers with no limit, exact fractions, and complex numbers.

-- A whole number simply keeps going. Nothing wraps round, nothing is thrown away.
please remember f is 1
please repeat for every n from 1 to 100:
    multiply f by n
thank you for repeating
please show "100 factorial is {f}"
please show "which is {the length of the text of f} digits long"

please show 2 to the power of 10
please remember big is the whole number in "123456789012345678901234567890" or 0
please show big times big

-- Fractions are exact, in a way decimals never are.
please show 1 over 3
please show 1 over 3 plus 1 over 3 plus 1 over 3
please show 1 over 2 plus 1 over 3
please show 6 over 8
please show the top of 6 over 8
please show the bottom of 6 over 8
please show 0.75 as a fraction
please show 1 over 3 as a decimal

-- Complex numbers, written the way they are read.
